// The points-to stage, field-insensitive: what Argus.Analysis.Extraction
// runs when even the selective stage (points_to_selective.dl) outgrows
// its budget. The same program, held to the same budget, with every
// object resolved by the field-insensitive pass (clientlib/hub_objects.dl),
// hub or not. The selective stage outgrows its budget where the
// program's terms merge into each other, each holding every other's
// fields through the helpers they are handed to, whatever objects they
// hold; the field-insensitive pass follows the objects alone, a row per
// variable an object reaches, so its rows grow with the variables and
// the objects, never with the terms. It writes the same relations,
// points_to_mode saying "field_insensitive", and every object as a hub
// (hub_object.csv).
//
// The stage modes are cumulative: this one is the selective stage with
// every object selected, so it holds stage_mode("selective") too.

.include "points_to.dl"

stage_mode("selective").
stage_mode("field_insensitive").
